WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.845
<v DANA>[playful] Let's talk about full sharps
containers. I'll admit, I've crammed one

00:00:04.845 --> 00:00:09.752
<v DANA>more thing into a kitchen trash can that
was already full. I even pushed it down

00:00:09.752 --> 00:00:10.560
<v DANA>with my hand.

00:00:10.560 --> 00:00:13.360
<v RAY>[dry] Well, a kitchen trash can is one
thing.

00:00:13.360 --> 00:00:16.320
<v DANA>So is a full sharps container any
different?

00:00:16.320 --> 00:00:21.172
<v RAY>It is, because a sharps container has a
fill line. Once the sharps reach that

00:00:21.172 --> 00:00:22.960
<v RAY>line, the container is FULL.

00:00:22.880 --> 00:00:27.713
<v DANA>[curious] So say it's right at the fill
line, but there's still a little gap at

00:00:27.713 --> 00:00:29.200
<v DANA>the top. Can you use it?

00:00:29.200 --> 00:00:34.318
<v RAY>No, you treat it as full and find another
designated container. If you push one

00:00:34.318 --> 00:00:38.320
<v RAY>more in, your hand ends up close to the
sharps already inside.

00:00:38.240 --> 00:00:43.440
<v DANA>Okay, that makes sense. Is a full
container the only thing to watch for?

00:00:43.360 --> 00:00:48.047
<v RAY>Actually, there's a second one, and it
looks NOTHING like the first. It's a

00:00:48.047 --> 00:00:50.960
<v RAY>sharp that ends up somewhere it doesn't
belong.

00:00:50.960 --> 00:00:53.200
<v DANA>Where would that be, usually?

00:00:53.200 --> 00:00:58.299
<v RAY>It could be on a work surface, hidden in
other material, or in the regular trash.

00:00:58.299 --> 00:01:03.334
<v RAY>Imagine someone tosses a used blade into
a regular trash bin, so the next person

00:01:03.334 --> 00:01:04.800
<v RAY>to reach in is at risk.

00:01:04.800 --> 00:01:10.521
<v DANA>So one hazard is a container that still
looks roomy, and the other is a sharp in

00:01:10.521 --> 00:01:11.680
<v DANA>the wrong place.

00:01:11.600 --> 00:01:17.040
<v RAY>Yes, and spotting either one early is how
you stop an injury before it happens.

00:01:17.040 --> 00:01:20.880
<v RAY>So the rule is this: at the fill line,
it's full.

00:01:20.880 --> 00:01:24.400
<v DANA>[laughs] My kitchen trash can could have
used a fill line.

